        "discipline": "Electrical and Computer",
        "subject": "Circuit Analysis",
        "chapter": "Node/Loop Analysis",
        "topic": "Mesh Analysis",
        "subtopic": "Overview",
        "content_html": "A specific use of KVL on a circuit is loop analysis. We utilize a particular form of loop called a \"mesh,\" which is a loop devoid of any other loops. A mesh begins at a node, travels around a circuit, and then returns to the starting node without ever seeing any nodes more than once. Only planar circuits, or circuits without crossover connections, can we apply mesh analysis on. Mesh analysis cannot be used if a circuit cannot be redrew without the intersecting unconnected lines.",
