        "discipline": "Electrical and Computer",
        "subject": "Electronics",
        "chapter": "OPAMP",
        "topic": "Ideal OPAMP",
        "subtopic": "Overview",
        "content_html": "<div class=\"container-fluid\">\r\n\t<div class=\"row align-items-start\">\r\n\t\t<div class=\"col col-lg-8\">\r\nAn ideal OPAMP has:\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Infinite input impedance</li>\r\n<li>Infinite bandwidth</li>\r\n<li>Infinite voltage gain</li>\r\n<li>Zero output impedance</li>\r\n<li>Zero power consumption</li>\r\n<ul>\r\n\r\n\t\t</div>\r\n    \t\t<div class=\"col\">\r\n     <center><img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/7d/Amplificatore_operazionale.svg\" alt=\"OPAMP\" width=\"340\"><br/>\r\n\r\n<small><small><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Amplificatore_operazionale.svg\">Giacomo Alessandroni</a>, <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\">CC BY-SA 4.0</a>, via Wikimedia Commons</small></small></center><br/>\r\n    \t\t</div>\r\n  \t</div>\r\n</div>",
