        "topic": "Indefinite Integrals",
        "subtopic": "Overview",
        "content_html": "<h5><span><b> List of Integration Formulae:</b></span></h5>\r\n\r\n\r\n<section id=\"services\" class=\"services\">\r\n  <div class=\"container-fluid\" data-aos=\"fade-up\">\r\n\r\n    <div class=\"row gy-3\">\r\n\r\n      <div class=\"col-lg-3\" data-aos=\"flip-left\" data-aos-delay=\"200\">\r\n        <div class=\"service-box orange\">\r\n          <h5><span><b>Algebraic:</b></span></h5>\r\n          <div class=\"text-center\">\r\n<p class=\"card-text\"><span class=\"math display\">\\[\\int x^n dx = \\dfrac {x^{n+1}}{n+1} + C\\]</span></p>\r\n          </div>\r\n        </div>\r\n      </div>\r\n\r\n      <div class=\"col-lg-3\" data-aos=\"flip-left\" data-aos-delay=\"800\">\r\n        <div class=\"service-box orange\">\r\n          <h5><span><b>Trigonometric:</b></span></h5>\r\n<p class=\"card-text\">\r\n  \\begin{align*}        \r\n\\int \\cos x\\ dx &= \\sin x + C\\\\\r\n\\int  \\sin x\\ dx &= -\\cos x+ C\\\\\r\n\\int \\sec^2 x \\ dx &= \\tan x + C\\\\\r\n\\int \\csc^2 x\\ dx &= - \\cot x  + C\\\\\r\n\\int  \\sec x \\tan x\\ dx &= \\sec x + C\\\\\r\n\\int  \\csc x \\cot x\\ dx &= -\\csc x  + C\\\\\r\n\\end{align*}\r\n</p>\r\n          \r\n        </div>\r\n      </div>\r\n\r\n      <div class=\"col-lg-3\" data-aos=\"flip-left\" data-aos-delay=\"1400\">\r\n        <div class=\"service-box orange\">\r\n          <h5><span><b>Log/Exp:</b></span></h5>\r\n<p class=\"card-text\">\r\n\\begin{align*}\r\n\\int e^x \\ dx &= e^x + C\\\\\r\n\\int a^x \\ dx&= \\dfrac{a^x}{\\log a} + C\\\\\r\n\\int \\dfrac{1}{x} \\ dx &= \\log x + C\r\n\\end{align*}\r\n</p>\r\n        </div>\r\n      </div>\r\n\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-lg-3\" data-aos=\"flip-left\" data-aos-delay=\"2000\">\r\n        <div class=\"service-box orange\">\r\n          <h5><span><b>Inv Trig:</b></span></h5>\r\n<p class=\"card-text\">\r\n  \\begin{align*}     \r\n\\int \\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{1-x^2}} \\ dx &= \\sin^{-1} x + C\\\\\r\n\\int \\dfrac{-1}{\\sqrt{1-x^2}} \\ dx &= \\cos^{-1} x + C\\\\\r\n\\int \\dfrac{1}{{1+x^2}} \\ dx &= \\tan^{-1} x + C\\\\ \r\n&= -\\cot^{-1} x + C\\\\\r\n\\int \\dfrac{1}{\\vert x \\vert \\sqrt{x^2 - 1}} \\ dx &= \\sec^{-1} x + C\\\\ \r\n&= -\\csc^{-1} x + C\r\n\\end{align*}\r\n</p>\r\n          \r\n        </div>\r\n      </div>\r\n\r\n    </div>\r\n  </div>\r\n</section>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<section id=\"services\" class=\"services\">\r\n  <div class=\"container-fluid\" data-aos=\"fade-up\">\r\n\r\n    <div class=\"row gy-4\">\r\n\r\n      <div class=\"col-lg-4\" data-aos=\"flip-left\" data-aos-delay=\"200\">\r\n        <div class=\"service-box orange\">\r\n          <h5><span><b>Integration by Substitution Method:</b></span></h5>\r\n          <div class=\"text-center\">\r\n<p class=\"card-text\"><span class=\"math display\"><p>There are occasions when it is possible to perform an apparently difficult piece of integration by first making a substitution. <span class=\"math display\">\\[I = \\int x \\sin (x^{2}+ 1)dx\\]</span> Substitute <span class=\"math display\">\\[(x^{2}+ 1) = u\\]</span> Then <span class=\"math display\">\\[2x dx= du\\]</span> or <span class=\"math display\">\\[x dx= \\dfrac{1}{2}du\\]</span> Then the integral becomes <span class=\"math display\">\\[\\begin{align*} I &amp;= \\dfrac{1}{2} \\int \\sin u du\\\\ &amp;= - \\dfrac{1}{2}\\ \\cos u = - \\dfrac{1}{2}\\ \\cos (x^{2}+ 1) + C\\end{align*}\\]</span></p></span></p>\r\n          </div>\r\n        </div>\r\n      </div>\r\n\r\n      <div class=\"col-lg-4\" data-aos=\"flip-left\" data-aos-delay=\"800\">\r\n        <div class=\"service-box orange\">\r\n          <h5><span><b>Integration by Parts:</b></span></h5>\r\n<p class=\"card-text\">\r\n<p><span class=\"math display\">\\[\\begin{align*} I = \\int x\\ \\cos x \\ dx &amp;= \\int u \\ dv\\\\ &amp;= uv - \\int v \\ du\\\\ &amp;= x\\ \\sin x - \\int \\sin x \\ dx\\\\ &amp;= x \\ \\sin x + \\cos x + C\\end{align*}\\]</span></p>\r\n</p>\r\n          \r\n        </div>\r\n      </div>\r\n\r\n      <div class=\"col-lg-4\" data-aos=\"flip-left\" data-aos-delay=\"1400\">\r\n        <div class=\"service-box orange\">\r\n          <h5><span><b>Integration by Partial Fractions:</b></span></h5>\r\n<p class=\"card-text\">\r\n<p>For partial fractions, the given fraction must be proper, i.e the highest degree of denominator polynomial must be higher than the highest degree of numerator polynomial. if not, first division must be carried out to make it a proper polynomial.</p>\r\n<ol>\r\n\t<li><span class=\"math inline\">\\(\\dfrac{3}{(x+2)(x+3)} = \\dfrac{A}{(x+2)} + \\dfrac{B}{(x+3)}\\)</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span class=\"math inline\">\\(\\dfrac{3}{(x+2)^2} = \\dfrac{A}{(x+2)} + \\dfrac{B}{(x+2)^2}\\)</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span class=\"math inline\">\\(\\dfrac{3}{(x^2+2)(x+3)} = \\dfrac{Ax + B}{(x^2+2)} + \\dfrac{C}{(x+3)}\\)</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span class=\"math inline\">\\(\\dfrac{3}{(x^2+2)(x+3)^2} = \\dfrac{Ax + B}{(x^2+2)} + \\dfrac{C}{(x+3)} + \\dfrac{D}{(x+3)^2}\\)</span></li>\r\n</ol>\r\n</p>\r\n        </div>\r\n      </div>\r\n\r\n    </div>\r\n  </div>\r\n</section>",
        "important": "",
        "resources": "<div class=\"mt-4 pt-4 border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 flex flex-wrap gap-2\"><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Cbor0EKETvWY1kFCwp7rhXIUtfNoxoPS/preview\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"px-3 py-1.5 bg-purple-100 dark:bg-purple-900/40 text-purple-700 dark:text-purple-300 rounded text-xs font-bold hover:bg-purple-200 transition-colors\">👨‍🏫 Tutoring</a><div class=\"w-full mt-2\"><div style=\"padding:57.88% 0 0 0;position:relative;\"><iframe allow=\"autoplay; fullscreen; picture-in-picture\" allowfullscreen=\"\" frameborder=\"0\" src=\"https://player.vimeo.com/video/580161459?badge=0&amp;autopause=0&amp;player_id=0&amp;app_id=58479\" style=\"position:absolute;top:0;left:0;width:100%;height:100%;\" title=\"Partial_Fractions\"></iframe></div>\r\n<script src=\"https://player.vimeo.com/api/player.js\"></script></div></div>",
        "images": [],
        "local_images": []
